# Godot Asset System

## Overview
- Asset discovery is provider-based: each `AssetProvider` subclasses `AssetProvider.gd`, emits `assets_changed`, and stays free of UI concerns.
- `AssetService.gd` is the sole entry point; it initializes providers at startup, runs scans, merges results, and broadcasts updates to consumers.
- Stable providers today are `FileSystemAssetProvider` (audio/MIDI files), `DeviceAssetProvider` (built-in and plugin devices), and `SfzAssetProvider` (SFZ sampler instruments).

## Asset & Provider Contracts
- `Asset.gd` wraps identity plus metadata (favorite, tags, last_used, size, modified time) and exposes helpers (`get_display_name`, type guards: `is_audio`, `is_midi`, `is_sfz`, `is_soundfont`).
- Asset types: `Audio` (audio files), `Midi` (MIDI files), `Device` (plugins/instruments), `SFZ` (SFZ instruments), `SoundFont` (SF2/SF3 instruments).
- Providers must populate `Asset.path` with an absolute file path or canonical device ID; `AssetService` keys on this value.
- Providers may opt into hot reload by setting `supports_hot_reload`; they are responsible for scheduling their own refresh loop.
- Change detection flows through the `assets_changed(added, removed, modified)` signal; AssetService reloads metadata and rebroadcasts.

## AssetService Autoload
- Reads `Sonara` config to determine enabled providers and scan paths, then calls `initialize(SceneTree)` on each provider.
- Providers emit cached assets during `initialize()` so `_assets_by_path` is populated via `assets_changed` callbacks before any live scan.
- **No automatic scan on startup** – relies on hot-reload timers for first scan (after `scan_interval_seconds`). Users can manually trigger via Edit → Scan Assets.
- `scan()` clears the registry, invokes `provider.scan()`, and consolidates every provider's `get_assets()` result into `_assets_by_path`.
- Metadata cache lives in `~/.config/sonara/assets.json`; the service loads it on startup, applies it to Assets, and persists on every write.
- Device-specific helpers (`get_device`, `get_instruments`, `get_effects`) proxy to the device provider, so providers must keep their registries authoritative.
- Manual plugin discovery goes through `scan_plugins()`, which delegates to the device provider and requires no additional UI wiring.

## FileSystemAssetProvider
- Honors `assets/samples/paths` and `assets/scan_interval_seconds` from config; `~/` is expanded to the user home.
- Supports audio (`wav`, `mp3`, `ogg`) and MIDI (`mid`, `midi`) extensions; all other files are ignored.
- Maintains `_file_mod_times` to detect additions, removals, and modifications, emitting a single aggregated change event per scan.
- Uses `SceneTree.create_timer()` for recurring scans; timers are chained so the provider never blocks `_ready()`.
- Caches discovered assets to `~/.config/sonara/samples_cache.json` for instant availability on startup.

## SfzAssetProvider
- Honors `assets/sfz/paths` and `assets/scan_interval_seconds` from config.
- Supports SFZ sampler instrument files (`.sfz` extension only); classified as `Asset.TYPE.SFZ` (distinct from regular audio files).
- Maintains `_file_mod_times` to detect changes identical to FileSystemAssetProvider pattern.
- Uses `SceneTree.create_timer()` for recurring scans with the same hot-reload architecture.
- Caches discovered SFZ files to `~/.config/sonara/sfz_cache.json` for instant availability on startup.
- SFZ files are loaded into the built-in sfizz device via `DeviceInstance.load_file()` method.
- Must be enabled in `assets/enabled_providers` array (default: `["filesystem", "devices", "sfz"]`).
- Browser UI displays SFZ assets in a dedicated "SFZ" tab with their own ItemList.

## DeviceAssetProvider
- On startup, loads cached plugins, registers OSC listeners, and immediately sends `/builtin/request`; the engine answers with `/builtin/info` messages (one per device) followed by `/builtin/complete`.
- Maintains `_devices` keyed by `device_id`; built-ins and plugins live in the same dictionary so `scan()` rebuilds the full asset list after every advertisement or scan completion.
- Plugin discovery is manual: `trigger_plugin_scan()` prunes cached plugin assets, then sends `/plugin/scan` via `AudioEngineOSC`.
- Incoming `/builtin/info` payloads include audio/MIDI capabilities, parameter descriptors, and optional file loading support; the provider batches new built-ins and emits them when `/builtin/complete` arrives.
- `/plugin/info` messages provide `[id, name, vendor, version, category, description, path]`; devices store metadata plus CLAP-specific fields.
- `/plugin/scan_complete` triggers `scan()`, emits added plugin assets, and persists the registry to `~/.config/sonara/plugins.json`.
- Cached plugins are reloaded on startup before the engine responds, so Browser UI stays populated even without a fresh scan; hot reconnects re-request built-ins by listening to `AudioEngineOSC.engine_connected`.

## Metadata Cache
- `AssetService` writes all user metadata (favorite, tags, last_used) to `assets.json` under the same config directory as the plugin cache.
- On provider change events, metadata is re-applied before signals propagate, so UI listeners always receive hydrated assets.
- Providers should avoid duplicating persistence logic; any additional metadata must route through AssetService to keep the cache consistent.
